          "source_quote": "τοῖς δὲ προλαβοῦσιν ὅτι θυσιῶν ὀρέγεται ὁ θεός",
          "english_quote": "To those who had asserted beforehand that God desires sacrifices",
          "issue": "προλαβοῦσιν here describes taking a position or forming an assumption beforehand. Unlike the preceding διαβεβαιουμένοις, it does not establish a confident verbal assertion. “Asserted” introduces an act of speech that the supplied wording does not establish; the note’s appeal to the following ὅτι clause does not resolve this distinction.",
          "suggested_revision": "Use “To those who had assumed beforehand that God desires sacrifices.” Revise the lexical note to explain the preconception sense and distinguish it from the preceding verb of confident assertion. The replacement requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἔφη „ὁ θεὸς ἔλεος θέλει καὶ οὐ θυσίας, ἐπίγνωσιν αὐτοῦ καὶ οὐχ ὁλοκαυτώματα.",
          "english_quote": "he said, “God wants mercy and not sacrifices, knowledge of him and not whole burnt offerings.”",
          "issue": "The supplied text also lacks a closing quotation mark after the final quotation. The existing source_issues entry discloses the English closure after ἐστίν, but not this additional closure. The boundary is intelligible; this is an editorial-punctuation disclosure issue, not evidence of missing wording.",
          "suggested_revision": "Extend source_issues to quote this final passage and disclose that the English supplies its closing quotation mark. Identify it as a punctuation feature of the supplied edition, without proposing lost words or requiring renewed print verification.",
