          "source_quote": "ὁ γὰρ ἀγαθὸς εἷς ἐστίν",
          "english_quote": "for the good is one",
          "issue": "The masculine singular substantive ὁ ἀγαθός, reinforced by masculine εἷς, denotes the good one or the one who is good. English “the good” ordinarily denotes an abstraction or a collective class, obscuring the personal singular construction. The lexical note explains the choice but does not make that English formulation sufficiently clear.",
          "suggested_revision": "Render “for the one who is good is one.” Preserve the unusual numerical predication rather than adding “God” or substituting a familiar canonical exclusion formula. Review the revised wording afresh.",
